    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Table&nbsp;4.01</span></strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> Histological differential diagnosis of iris melanoma</span></p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Hardeep Singh Mudhar",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.8pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Diagnosis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 216.7pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"289\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Histological features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Immunohistochemistry</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 63.45pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"85\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Molecular features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.75pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Other features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.05pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"93\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">References</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Iris melanoma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 216.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"289\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <em>Histopathology</em> in <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;3.1.2.4&gt;&gt;</span><em>Iris melanoma</em></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <em>Histopathology</em> in <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;3.1.2.4&gt;&gt;</span><em>Iris melanoma</em></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 63.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"85\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <em>Diagnostic molecular pathology</em> in <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;3.1.2.4&gt;&gt;</span><em>Iris melanoma</em></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">None</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"93\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;3.1.2.4&gt;&gt;</span><em>Iris melanoma</em></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.8pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Iris naevus</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 216.7pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"289\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Melanocytic cells are commonly spindle shaped with fusiform nuclei, dispersed chromatin, and indistinct regular basophilic nucleoli</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">The nucleus may be grooved and show pseudoinclusions</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">The cytoplasm can be variably pigmented</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Naevus cells can be ovoid or polyhedral</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Stroma can be sclerotic</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">The iris vessels are usually not effaced</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">BAP1 is retained</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 63.45pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"85\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">GNAQ</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">, <em>GNA11</em>, <em>EIF1AX</em>, <em>NRAS</em>, <em>PTEN</em>, <em>KIT</em>, and <em>TP53</em> mutations</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.75pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Tumour seeding into iris stroma and anterior chamber angle with secondary glaucoma can occur</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Malignant transformation to melanoma can occur</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.05pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"93\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{7305709;28700778;29371009;35835335}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Iris melanocytoma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 216.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"289\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Plump polyhedral melanocytic cells with abundant heavily pigmented cytoplasm that commonly obscures the nucleus</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">After bleaching, small round to oval nuclei, with regular basophilic small nucleoli, and finely dispersed chromatin</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No mitotic figures</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Necrosis can be present</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">n/a</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 63.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"85\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">GNAQ</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> or <em>GNA11</em> mutations</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Tumour seeding into iris stroma and anterior chamber angle with secondary glaucoma can occur</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Malignant transformation to melanoma can occur</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"93\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{15767055;2777104;17947283;19484449}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.8pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Iris melanocytosis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 216.7pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"289\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Heavily pigmented spindle, fusiform, or multipolar/dendritic melanocytic cells resembling normal iris stromal melanocytes, dispersed in non-sclerotic stroma or forming cell process tangles</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Stroma contains melanophages</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No mitotic figures and no cytological atypia</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">n/a</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 63.45pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"85\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">GNA11</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> or <em>GNAQ</em> mutations in association with cutaneous melanocytosis and phakomatosis pigmentovascularis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.75pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Iris melanocytosis can be isolated or part of oculodermal melanocytosis</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Melanocytoma can occur within iris melanocytosis</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Iris melanoma transformation within melanocytosis can occur</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.05pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"93\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;3.1.2.1&gt;&gt;</span><em>Ocular melanocytosis</em></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{10900118;848534;7743806;18572057;19770714}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.8pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Ciliary body melanoma with anterior extension</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 216.7pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"289\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Atypical spindle and/or epithelioid melanocytic cells with mitotic activity</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <em>Histopathology</em> in <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;3.2.2.1&gt;&gt;</span></span><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Choroidal and ciliary body melanomas</span></em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <em>Histopathology</em> in <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;3.2.2.1&gt;&gt;</span><em>Choroidal and ciliary body melanomas</em></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 63.45pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"85\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <em>Diagnostic molecular pathology</em> in <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;3.2.2.1&gt;&gt;</span></span><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Choroidal and ciliary body melanomas</span></em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.75pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Not relevant</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.05pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"93\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;3.2.2.1&gt;&gt;</span></span><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Choroidal and ciliary body melanomas</span></em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><a name=\"_Hlk198645719\"></a><span lang=\"EN-GB\">n/a, not applicable.</span></p>",
